{"duration_api_ms":190551,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"be926d42-0e72-4b82-9a66-a7987dcb7340","total_cost_usd":0.239066,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14503,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18105,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":12750},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14503,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":18105,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14503,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14503},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":18105,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14503,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.239066,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":12750,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"All 9 front points sit on one cone=70 (upper bound) curve with D about 3.3-3.38 and b 1.0-1.25. Flight-path angle then trades heat flux (250-290 kW/m2) against bondline temperature (394-422 K). Bondline temperature is the axis that pays: 1 K is worth about 0.006 normalised hypervolume, while a 5% cut in heat flux is worth about 0.002. Three things bound the front. Mass margin depends only on D, b and cone (identical margins across gammas at D 3.3, b 1.2), and it caps D near 3.385. g depends on gamma and weakly on D, not on b or cone, and caps gamma near -3.6. Bluntness only helps, so b should go to its 1.35 maximum. Cone below 70 only adds mass (C-ffcd43d3a722), so it is not worth exploring.\",\"evidence\":[\"Mass margin at D 3.3 is 0.0445 (b 1.0, C-a3e754710f53), 0.0497 (b 1.2, C-6041504dc2c9) and 0.0512 (b 1.25, C-b49265f1a558). D 3.38/b 1.25 gives 0.0046 (C-e8cf251744f0) and D 3.45 gives -0.037 (C-2439bd64c673). This puts the D limit near 3.385 at b 1.35.\",\"g at D 3.3, b 1.2, gamma -3.5 is 11.806 for b 0.9 (C-c9ba8204e0d2) and b 1.2 (C-6041504dc2c9), so g is independent of b. g rises about 1.64 per degree of gamma (C-b460a0993d3f, C-26ab72164762) and about 0.4 per metre of D (C-e8cf251744f0). At D 3.375, gamma -3.58 should give about 11.97, under the limit of 12.\",\"C-e8cf251744f0 (D 3.38, gamma -3.5) has q 288k and T 394.06, against 300.9k and 395.8 K for D 3.3 (C-6041504dc2c9). Larger D is therefore better on both objectives, and the shallow-gamma front points still at D 3.3 can be improved the same way.\",\"C-2439bd64c673 at D 3.45 shows T about 393.8 K even at gamma -3.4, so larger D lowers T by roughly 19 K/m.\",\"C-ffcd43d3a722 (cone 66) has a smaller mass margin than a cone-70 design of the same size, and its g matches the D/gamma scaling. The other eight failures are geometry failures, all at cone <= 60, so cone 70 is both safe and lightest.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak heat flux scales roughly as D^-1.5 and b^-0.2, and depends weakly on gamma. Bondline temperature follows heat load, which falls with larger nose radius (b*D), lower ballistic coefficient (larger D) and steeper entry. The active constraints are mass fraction (upper limit on D, eased slightly by b) and g (limit on steepness). The best design is therefore D about 3.375-3.39, b 1.35, cone 70, with gamma swept from -1.5 to about -3.6 to fill the front. Predictions extrapolate the fitted D, b and gamma trends from the tables, with b^-0.2 and the D exponent taken from a few point comparisons.\",\"uncertainty\":\"b above 1.25 is untested. The heat-flux gain from b may saturate, and mass margin may bend nonlinearly near D 3.385-3.39. g is close to 12 at gamma -3.58 to -3.6, and its D dependence is estimated from only a few points. The absolute T and q predictions carry about 1-2 K and 2-3% error.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-b49265f1a558\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow end of the front with larger D and b 1.35 to lower q. It uses the maximum-b, near-maximum-D recipe.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":237000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":420.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front to the lowest-q corner at the gamma bound and tests b 1.35.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9f787a9a1c79\",\"rationale\":\"Replaces the D 3.3 point at gamma -1.8 with D 3.375, b 1.35, which should be better on both objectives.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":243500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":415.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves the shallow front by about 5% in q and 2 K in T.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3a1c0a2c81ce\",\"rationale\":\"Fills the gamma -2.1 gap with the improved D/b recipe.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":250000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a mid-front slot with a design that should dominate the D 3.3 neighbours.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ed0654b17260\",\"rationale\":\"Same recipe at gamma -2.4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":257000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves the mid-front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ed0654b17260\",\"rationale\":\"Slot at gamma -2.55 between the -2.4 and -2.7 points.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":260500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills front spacing at low risk.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-688d3d0406c7\",\"rationale\":\"Same recipe at gamma -2.7.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":264600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves the mid-front over C-688d3d0406c7.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-2ea60b1a89b3\",\"rationale\":\"Slot at gamma -2.9 with the improved D/b.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the front between gamma -2.8 and -3.0.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-2ea60b1a89b3\",\"rationale\":\"Same recipe at gamma -3.0, replacing the D 3.3, b 1.2 point.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Should dominate C-2ea60b1a89b3 (287.8k, 401.3 K).\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a51f1ded896c\",\"rationale\":\"Same recipe at gamma -3.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves the steep-mid front, where T gains are most valuable.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e8cf251744f0\",\"rationale\":\"Same recipe at gamma -3.35.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.35},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":280000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the front between -3.2 and -3.5; g is about 11.7, so it should be safe.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e8cf251744f0\",\"rationale\":\"Same recipe at gamma -3.45, with g about 11.85 (safe).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":283000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves on C-e8cf251744f0 (288k, 394.06 K) in q and T.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e8cf251744f0\",\"rationale\":\"Same recipe at gamma -3.52, g about 11.9.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.52},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":285000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Approaches the g limit safely while lowering T.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e8cf251744f0\",\"rationale\":\"Steep, T-optimised point: gamma -3.58 with D 3.375, b 1.35. Predicted g is about 11.97 against the limit of 12.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.58},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":286000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Targets the lowest-T corner of the front, worth about 0.008 hypervolume if it holds.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e8cf251744f0\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly larger D 3.38 with b 1.35 at gamma -3.58, giving margin to test the mass boundary.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.58},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":285000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Distinguishes the D effect from the b effect at the steep corner.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e8cf251744f0\",\"rationale\":\"Probes the mass limit at D 3.385 with b 1.35, gamma -3.55. Mass margin is predicted at about +0.004.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":285000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the D ceiling with b 1.35.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e8cf251744f0\",\"rationale\":\"Pushes D to 3.39 to bracket the mass limit. Predicted margin is only about +0.001.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.39,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":284500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether the mass margin is nonlinear near the limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e8cf251744f0\",\"rationale\":\"Tests the bluntness effect: b 1.3 at D 3.375, gamma -3.58, to see whether the heat-flux benefit of b saturates.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.3,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.58},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":287000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Compared with the b 1.35 twin, it isolates the b effect on q and T.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e8cf251744f0\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly steeper gamma -3.59 at D 3.375, b 1.35. Predicted g is about 11.98, which is marginal.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.59},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":286500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the g boundary to fix the steepest usable gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-26ab72164762\",\"rationale\":\"Lower-D, safe-mass steep point (D 3.3, b 1.35, gamma -3.6) with g predicted at 11.97, to test the b 1.35 gain at the steepest angle.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":297000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the steep edge with a larger mass margin, and checks the gamma -3.6 g limit at D 3.3.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":147606,"type":"result","duration_ms":190580,"uuid":"069f03f5-d2f7-4d6f-9711-ea1a380eb4f6","ttft_stream_ms":1145,"time_to_request_ms":27,"first_content_frame_ms":1146,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
